          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "Neutrino oscillation experiments have entered a precision era. The determination of the leptonic charge-parity (CP)-violating phase, the resolution of the neutrino mass ordering, and the increasingly stringent tests of the three-flavour paradigm all rest on comparing measured event rates against predictions at the percent level [@T2K:2025wet; @NOvA:2025tmb; @DUNE:2020jqi; @Hyper-Kamiokande:2025fci]. Because",
      "extractCut": true
    },
