      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro_diffprog label=\"sec:intro_diffprog\"} Differentiable programming makes a simulation differentiable in its own inputs, so that derivatives of the prediction are produced by the program rather than reconstructed outside it. Automatic differentiation [@Baydin:2015tfa] decomposes a program into elementary operations and applies the chain rule through each of them, giving the exact derivative of the output",
      "extractCut": true
    },
